.TH ONEDRIVE-ONDEMAND-UNMOUNT 1 "October 2026" "onedrive-ondemand" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
onedrive-ondemand-unmount \- remove a stale Files On-Demand mount of a onedrive profile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B onedrive-ondemand-unmount
[\fB\-\-confdir=\fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads \fBsync_dir\fR from \fIDIR/config\fR (default
\fI~/.config/onedrive-ondemand\fR; \fI~/OneDrive\fR when the config does not
set it) and, if the onedrive FUSE file system (fuse.onedrive) is still mounted there, unmounts it with
\fBfusermount3 \-u \-z\fR. Nothing mounted is not an error. The
onedrive-ondemand systemd user units run it as \fBExecStopPost=\fR.
The client also unmounts a stale mount itself when it starts. Only the
mount is removed; the downloaded files in \fBsync_dir\fR underneath stay.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-confdir=\fIDIR\fR
Profile directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Only report what would be done.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR onedrive (1),
.BR onedrive-ondemand-setup (1),
.BR fusermount3 (1)
